# Accepted memcheck reports for the taint harness. Each entry is a
# secret-dependent access or branch that the design documents and accepts;
# scripts/ct-taint.sh fails on anything not listed here. Add an entry only
# with a reason. Frame names are demangled Rust symbols, matched as globs.

# `oblivious_lookup` rejects an out-of-range index before the constant-time
# scan, and its callers test the `Result`. The comparison is against the
# public table length, and every symbol the encryptors produce is in range,
# so the branch direction is the same for every input and carries no
# information; it is still a comparison on the plaintext symbol, which is
# why memcheck reports it. Removing it means an infallible `permute` over a
# typed in-domain symbol.
{
   oblivious-lookup-range-check
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:*oblivious_lookup*
}
{
   oblivious-lookup-range-check-result
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:*branch<u8*PrpError*
}
